Project AI coding rules (RSG-first):

Always follow these files in this exact order before generating code:
1) RSG_UNIFIED_REGULATION.md
2) RSG_UNIFIED_NATIVE_FUNCTIONS.md
3) RSG_UNIFIED_FUNCTION_NATIVE_INDEX.json
4) CURSOR_RSG_RULESET.md
5) RSG_ZERO_TO_SCRIPT_PLAYBOOK.md

Legacy references (fallback only, keep compatibility):
- RSG_ORG_FUNCTION_INDEX.json
- RSG_ORG_REGULAMENT_ABSOLUT_COMPLET.md
- RSG_ORG_REGULAMENT_COMPLET.md
- RSG_DOCS_REGULAMENT_SUPLIMENTAR.md
- RSG_DOCS_AUDIT_INDEX.json
- RSG_NATIVE_CATALOG.md

Mandatory behavior:
- Reuse existing RSG patterns/functions/events from the indexed files when available.
- Do not invent alternative flows if an RSG model already exists.
- Keep sensitive validation server-side only.
- Never process money/item rewards on client side.
- Prefer RSG APIs and exports (rsg-core, rsg-inventory, callbacks, prompts, statebags).
- Use only native patterns allowed by RSG_NATIVE_CATALOG.md.
- Respect deprecated/forbidden patterns documented in CURSOR_RSG_RULESET.md.
- Prefer callbacks for request-response flows and events for one-way flows.
- Respect lifecycle patterns: OnPlayerLoaded for init and OnPlayerUnload for cleanup.
- Use StateBags for frequently-read live status sync; avoid event/callback spam in loops.
- Use mandatory resource file structure:
  - `fxmanifest.lua` (root)
  - `config.lua` (root)
  - `client/client.lua`
  - `server/server.lua`
  - `locales/ro.lua`
- All user-facing texts must be centralized in `locales/ro.lua`.
- Romanian locale text must be written without Romanian diacritics.
- In `config.lua`, every configurable line must include an inline comment on the same line (not above/below).
- Keep `config.lua` clean and ordered by sections (General, NPC/Locations, Jobs, Economy, Security, UI/Blips, Debug).
- Scope must be strict to the request:
  - If user asks only "add NPC", implement only NPC-related changes.
  - If user asks only "modify NPC blip name", change only blip/name-related config/code.
  - Do not add unrelated systems, helpers, events, callbacks, commands, or dependencies.
  - Use only relevant functions/natives for the requested feature in config/client/server.

When user provides server rules/regulation:
- Convert each rule into technical checks (permission, distance, item/money validation, cooldown, logs).
- Apply those checks in server code paths.

When building from scratch:
- Follow staged implementation from RSG_ZERO_TO_SCRIPT_PLAYBOOK.md.
- Implement incrementally (function by function), preserving existing code.
